{
    "name": "E2E RoomPriceGenie - trigger new restriction update",
    "description": "Waits for a minimum stay update that RoomPriceGenie pushes for the connected sandbox property (New Restriction Update). Needs a manual step in the RoomPriceGenie account.",
    "notes": {
        "61f8d335-53c1-4dfa-be69-bd9fa0d00aab": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 336,
            "width": 880,
            "height": 320,
            "content": "## Never run\n\nThis flow was written from RoomPriceGenie's documentation and has only passed `appmixer e2e validate`. No RoomPriceGenie test account existed when it was written. See README.md in this folder for what a run needs.\n\n## ⚠️ Manual step: only RoomPriceGenie can fire this trigger\n\nEvery update is signed by RoomPriceGenie and the connector verifies the signature, so the flow cannot send itself a test update. While the flow runs (it waits 10 minutes):\n\n1. Open the RoomPriceGenie sandbox account of the connected property. Minimum stay must be enabled for the integration (ask RoomPriceGenie).\n2. Set a minimum stay of 2 nights on a date in the next 7 days and upload it (the documentation does not name the button for restrictions; ask RoomPriceGenie if **Upload Prices** does not send it).\n\nBefore that, once: RoomPriceGenie must have the endpoint `<API URL of this instance>/plugins/appmixer/roompricegenie/events` registered for your partner account in the same environment as the connector configuration, and the connected property must have its rooms mapped (flow \"E2E RoomPriceGenie - inventory\") and prices sent (flow \"E2E RoomPriceGenie - ari updates\").\n\nOne upload covers several room types; the trigger fires once for each, so the Assert may run more than once."
        }
    },
